__normal.jpg", "displayName": "Scott Turner", "username": "SecretaryTurner"}, "content": "The \u201cMixed Status\u201d loophole allowed illegal aliens to simply declare U.S. citizenship to gain HUD housing with no proof of eligibility.\n\nNow we require the documentation.\n\nEligible tenants and American citizens only.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 3207}, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 73, "created": 1794596128000, "id": "2121316031557939230", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2070499958919245824/CbmXzm4S_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Department of Housing and Urban Development", "username": "HUDgov"}, "content": "Under the final rule, individuals who declare U.S. citizenship must provide proof such as a U.S. birth certificate or naturalization certificate. \n\nBefore, proof wasn\u2019t required.", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 1315}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}], "status": true}